+# Ecosystem agent instructions
+
+This repository is the canonical ecosystem governance and public portfolio source. Before any ecosystem assignment, read docs/ECOSYSTEM_ARCHITECTURE.md and the current owning repository instructions. Reuse existing implementations, reviews and unpublished work; do not restart assignments.
+
+## Design and onboarding — owner direction, 28 October 2026
+
+- Follow the design/onboarding section in docs/ECOSYSTEM_ARCHITECTURE.md. One main stylesheet per owned application/site, with one maintained source of truth. Tokens → shared components → minimal justified page exceptions. Do not force independent products into a shared runtime or copy drifting themes across repositories.
+- Adapt Material 3 to approved brand guidelines. Readable tracking and line height, balanced gutters, semantic labels, accessible text/surface pairs, keyboard focus and responsive layouts are required. Do not compress every heading or introduce competing theme settings.
+- State the intended audience and one first useful task. Keep source, attribution, permission, uncertainty and manual handoff limits visible. Do not present synthetic records as live results.
+- Holdings is the owner-directed business/command review surface for Creator OS results on the Atmosphere; Made-Sick owns its join flow. This is product direction, not proof of implemented report ingestion, cross-site accounts, automatic publication or a VR/metaverse runtime.
+- Preserve the current project scope. A reference or relationship does not authorize changes to another product. Do not transfer private data, identity or consent flags through URLs.
+- Update authoritative brand guidelines and the change record. Create reviewable changes and a verified Vercel preview before release. Do not merge, publish or change production configuration until Dominique explicitly authorizes that release.
+- Report code, deployed behavior and physical iPad/Safari/VoiceOver verification separately. Passing browser emulation or tests is not physical-device acceptance.
+
+Local portfolio design choices are recorded in docs/PORTFOLIO_DESIGN.md. These instructions do not authorize migrations or changes to unrelated project code.
