+## Shared design and onboarding principles — owner direction, 28 October 2026
+
+These principles apply to all agents working on the ecosystem; each owning repository retains its implementation and release authority. Inspect current instructions, open assignments and existing brand guidelines first. A shared principle is not authorization to modify every project.
+
+**Audience and purpose.** Holdings is PIXIE’s business-facing, command-led review surface for people inspecting the results of Creator OS work on the Atmosphere. Made-Sick is the existing community/join destination. This updates intended audience positioning; it does not establish a connected report pipeline, a shipped CLI, shared accounts, membership or automatic publication. The original AetherOS design reference is owner-supplied lineage, not a shared runtime or affiliation. The Metaverse business article is contextual reference, not a claim that the AT Protocol Atmosphere is VR.
+
+**Top-down design.** Each owned site/application has one authoritative main stylesheet and a maintained source of truth: semantic tokens first, shared typography/components second, the smallest justified page exception last. Avoid inline/page/injected style systems, stacked theme overrides and independently maintained copies. Essential runtime window position, visibility and canvas dimensions are interaction state, not separate design themes. Separate products retain their identities; do not impose a cross-domain CSS dependency or shared runtime merely to satisfy consistency.
+
+**Material and brand.** Adapt Material 3 foundations for typography roles, color pairs, interaction states, shape and responsive layout to the approved brand guidelines. The PIXIE palette is midnight #071923, velvet plum #211823, slate #354955, mist #93999F, parchment #F2E5CE, aged gold #D5AB68 and glacial teal #A9E2E5. Readable semantic variants are allowed. Guiding Star, Winged Spark and PIXIE Cameo are complementary approved identity directions; do not fabricate a chronology or replace them arbitrarily. Prefer normal, readable heading spacing and line height, balanced container gutters, clear label semantics, visible keyboard focus, sufficient contrast and usable touch targets. Avoid bright beige backgrounds, compressed letters, oversized panels with narrow left-aligned text and competing page-level settings.
+
+**Onboarding.** Explain who a surface serves and demonstrate one useful task: result → evidence → next action. Prefer clear sample content, command help with accessible button equivalents and progressive disclosure over a tour of every subsystem. Keep originals, provenance, permission, rights and uncertainty attached. Distinguish sample, proposed, implemented and verified states. Joining occurs through the owning service’s explicit sign-in/consent flow; never infer membership from opening a page or move identity/consent/private report content in URLs.
+
+**Review and record.** Register changes in existing authoritative brand guidelines; label proposed designs and outstanding verification. Provide a tested Vercel preview before owner release review. Do not merge to main, promote, publish, alter domains or change hosting configuration without explicit authorization for that release. Report source changes, preview readiness, live behavior and physical iPad/Safari/VoiceOver acceptance separately. Apply these instructions through each repository’s normal review path; do not claim that every external repository or installed agent has been updated automatically.
